  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have, \\(2 x \\frac{d y}{d x}=y+3 \\Rightarrow \\frac{2}{y+3} d y=\\frac{d x}{x}\\) integrating, \\(2 \\ln (y+3)=\\ln x+\\ln c=\\ln c x\\)\n\\(\\Rightarrow \\ln (y+3)^2=\\ln \\mathrm{cx} \\Rightarrow(y+3)^2=\\mathrm{cx}\\)\nwhich is a family of parabolas.",
    "image": null
